course: dictionary
lesson: 15776
title: The word tutu
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name things you would only see in one kind of place. A tutu is one of them. Read the words around it to find its meaning: «Mia put on her pink tutu before the ballet show.» Ballet is dancing, and a skirt worn for a dance show must be a dancing costume, so a tutu is a skirt for dancing.
explain: The clues in «The dancers spun across the stage in their stiff, frilly tutus.» tell you what the skirt looks like. Stiff and frilly mean it does not hang down softly but sticks out.
explain: The word can also mean a light, puffy net skirt for dressing up. «At the party, Sam wore a tutu and a sparkly crown.» Here it is not for real ballet but part of a fun costume. Ask: what word would fit here? A skirt, a costume, a dress-up outfit. Swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A tutu is a kind of skirt.
fact: «Tutu» means a short, stiff, frilly skirt that sticks out, worn by ballet dancers.
fact: «Tutu» can also mean a light, puffy net skirt that children wear for dressing up.
fact: Tutus appear at dance shows, fancy-dress parties and fun runs, where people wear them as a joke.
fact: The plural of tutu is tutus, as in «Three tutus hung on the door.»
exercise: «Mia put on her pink tutu before the ballet show.» What is a tutu here? | *A stiff, frilly skirt worn by ballet dancers | A bag for carrying shoes | A pink hat for the stage | A pair of ballet shoes
exercise: «At the party, Sam wore a tutu and a sparkly crown.» Why was Sam wearing a tutu? | A hat for the sun | *For dressing up, as part of a fun costume | To go swimming in the sea | To carry books to school
exercise: Find and copy the word that means skirts for dancing in this sentence: «The dancers spun across the stage in their stiff, frilly tutus.» | spun | frilly | stage | *tutus
test: «The tutu sticks out when she twirls.» What does sticks out suggest about the tutu? | It hangs down limp like a wet towel | It is hidden under her coat | It is made of wood | *It stands out stiffly from the waist
test: Ruby says a tutu is a kind of jumper. Why is she wrong? | Jumpers are always pink | A tutu is a jumper for winter | Ruby is right, it is a jumper | *A tutu is a skirt, not a jumper
exam: «Tom wore a tutu to the fun run.» Which meaning of tutu fits best here? | *A light, puffy skirt for dressing up | A tall hat for the rain | A pair of running shoes | A dark, heavy coat
